functor: 1
title: turn
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`turn` · reflect · a dual or opposite.

# Form

`x.turn` on a symbol, `(a + b).turn` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `A.turn` | $A.turn$ | font glyph U+2200 |
| `Sigma.turn` | $Sigma.turn$ | built and cached |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A dual or opposite. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | Use a `sym` to give a recipe a short name. |
| Construction | A mirror image or a half turn of the base. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.

# From LaTeX

`\forall` is `forall`, and also `A.turn`.

